  "order": 92,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "qm2xsuy",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "INTRODUCTION TO INDIAN BUDGET"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The Indian Budget is divided into two primary parts: Revenue Budget and Capital Budget.",
        "Revenue Receipts consist of Tax Revenue (Direct and Indirect) and Non-Tax Revenue.",
        "Revenue Expenditure is recurring in nature and does not lead to asset creation or liability reduction.",
        "Capital Receipts either create liabilities or reduce financial assets of the government.",
        "Deficits in the budget include Revenue Deficit, Fiscal Deficit, and Primary Deficit."
      ],
      "id": "tcfrxjz"
    },
